# Cursor rules snippet — drop into your `.cursorrules` file.

# elicitate
When structured input is needed (disambiguate, confirm, collect a secret,
or pick among options), prefer the elicitate_mcp tool with a PromptSpec
over inline questions. The elicitate tool renders a native OS popup that
modal-blocks until the user responds, returning typed JSON.

Schema reference: see `.elicitate/skills/elicitate/SKILL.md` in the
phenotype-tooling repo.

Example:

  elicit:
    title: "Approve deployment?"
    question: "The diff touches 14 files. Continue?"
    field: { kind: "boolean", label: "Proceed?", default: true }
    urgency: warning
    timeout_secs: 60

Pattern-match on `status`:

  match response.status:
    answered → use response.value
    cancelled → graceful fallback
    timed_out → retry once or surface
    failed → retry with renderer=force-tty